# Keep optional creative changes, replacements, and enhancements inside mods

Keep optional creative changes, replacements, and enhancements inside mods.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Keep optional creative changes, replacements, and enhancements inside
  mods.

## Dependencies

No explicit task dependency was recorded in the legacy TODO.

## Evidence

The accepted [faithful-base governance ADR](../../../adr/governance/faithful-base-and-optional-mod-boundary.md)
assigns new/redesigned missions, worlds, geometry, textures, audio, UI, balance,
abilities, presentation, quality-of-life behavior, replacement media, and other
non-parity enhancements to SHAR mods. A mod can use registered extension and
replacement points but cannot become evidence for canonical base identity.

The existing drop-in mod ADR and platform extension contract provide the
reviewable package, activation, replacement, rollback, and conflict boundaries
for that optional work. `AGENTS.md` now points agents and operators at the same
faithful-base decision so AI-assisted authoring cannot silently promote a
creative mod change into base reconstruction.
